<title>HUNGARY: EBRD to convert loan to Hungary K&amp;H bank to stake.</title>
<headline>EBRD to convert loan to Hungary K&amp;H bank to stake.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) is likely to convert a $30 million subordinated loan to Hungary's  Kereskedelmi es Hitelbank Rt (K&amp;H) bank into a 17 percent stake in the bank by the end of the year, an official of Belgium's Kredietbank told the daily Magyar Hirlap.</p>
<p>&quot;After that, the Kredietbank and Irish Life (Plc) consortium will have 48 percent and the EBRD 17 percent in the bank,&quot; Kredietbank director for Central and Eastern Europe Luc Flamee said.</p>
<p>The consortium won a bid for a 10 percent, or nominal one billion forints, stake in K&amp;H for $30 million in July.</p>
<p>According to a privatisation contract, to be signed on Thursday, the consortium will also raise the bank's capital by $60 million at 105 percent of the face value later this year.</p>
<p>Flamee added that the state's shares in K&amp;H will be listed on the bourse.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
